<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">British South Africa Company</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> Company was a chartered company founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-rhodes">Cecil Rhodes</a> in 1889 to acquire and exploit territory in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. It occupied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwe plateau</a> in 1890, creating the colony later named Rhodesia. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shona">Shona</a> resistance to its rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-chimurenga">First Chimurenga</a> of 1896–1897 drew on organisational traditions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company.jpg" alt="British South Africa Company" width="320" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_British_South_Africa_Company.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
